<Base title="Privacy Policy | The Soft Nest Edit" description="Learn what browser data The Soft Nest Edit uses and how outbound retailer links work.">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="shell"><span class="eyebrow">VISITOR INFORMATION</span><h1>Privacy <em>policy.</em></h1><p>A straightforward description of how our affiliate-focused website handles information.</p></div></section>
  <div class="shell info-page"><p><strong>Effective date:</strong> November 20, 2026</p><p>This policy describes the default site included in the v2 project. Review and customize it before publication, particularly if you enable analytics, add forms, or operate in a jurisdiction with additional privacy requirements.</p><h2>Saved products</h2><p>When you use the Saved feature, product identifiers are stored in your browser's local storage. They are not uploaded to our server. Clearing your browser data removes them.</p><h2>Hosting and technical information</h2><p>Our hosting provider may process technical requests, IP addresses, and error logs to deliver and protect the site. Some editorial photographs are hosted on Unsplash, and loading them makes a request to that service.</p><h2>Analytics</h2><p>{site.webAnalyticsToken ? 'We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to understand general visits and website performance. See Cloudflare’s policies for more details.' : 'The default site does not enable a third-party analytics script. Analytics may be added later after this policy is updated.'}</p><h2>Affiliate links</h2><p>Clicking an Amazon product link takes you to Amazon, which has its own cookies, privacy policy, and order processing practices. We do not receive your payment card details through this website.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>For privacy questions, use the contact method shown on our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>. This policy is a starting template and does not replace legal advice.</p></div>
</Base>
